┌ ┌ minecraft-flk ─ actions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ ┐
│ │ d  deploy         build the image and roll machines to a new release     │ │
│ │ r  roll back      back to an older release's image and config, rolled o… │ │
│ │ c  scale          set the number of machines                             │ │
│ │ u  resume         nothing to resume                                      │ │
│ │ S  stop all       stop its running machines; resume brings them back     │ │
│ │ e  set secret     set a secret; the value goes to flk on stdin, never o… │ │
│ │ U  unset secret   no secrets                                             │ │
│ │ n  new volume     create a volume for [[mounts]] source = NAME           │ │
│ │ i  import volume  register an existing ext4 image; flk never deletes it  │ │
│ │ b  back up        copy all of minecraft-flk's volumes to the backup dir… │ │
│ │ l  logs           follow all its machines' console output                │ │
│ │ D  destroy app    delete the app, its machines, releases and volumes     │ │
│ │ 1  who            who's online (RCON)                                    │ │
│ │ 2  say            broadcast a message to the players (RCON)              │ │
│ │ 3  save           write the world to disk now and wait until it's saved  │ │
│ │ 4  backup         the nightly backup, now: live (no restart, ~25s), che… │ │
│ │ 5  backup-check   preflight only: mounts, flk, lock, status; makes no b… │ │
│ │ 6  whitelist      let a player in: type their name (RCON)                │ │
├ │                                                                          │─┤
│ │ build the image and roll machines to a new release                       │ │
├─│ $ flk -a minecraft-flk deploy                                            │─┤
│ ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤ │
